# This app's R8 keep rules. It is a `keepRules` source set (AGP 9.3+), so every `.keep` file here is
# picked up with no `proguardFiles` entry naming it. It sits in `main` rather than `release` so the
# opt-in `-PminifyDebug` build, which a device lane will run (#11), minifies against the same rules as
# release; a per-variant copy is the one that goes stale.
#
# OkHttp, DataStore and kotlinx.serialization ship their own consumer rules, and so does
# binge-companions' contracts module: its META-INF/proguard rule keeps the fields of every contract
# message, which the lite protobuf runtime looks up by name. R8 reads it even though the contracts
# arrive through the composite build. Jellyfin's responses are read as JsonElement trees, never
# through @Serializable classes, so there is no DTO to keep. Only what this app
# genuinely needs on top of those belongs here: a rule copied from a library silently diverges when
# the library is upgraded.

# Line numbers and source file names, so a crash a user reports reads as a stack trace.
-keepattributes SourceFile,LineNumberTable
-renamesourcefileattribute SourceFile
